warning[VITA-W1017] W-PP-TIMESCALE-DEFAULT: no `timescale in the design; assuming the 1ns/1ns base
kx_fdflt_own.sv:11:33: error[VITA-E3009] E-ELAB-UNSUPPORTED: function `f2` has an output/inout formal, so its copy-out has to be emitted as a statement before the expression that calls it. That works in any position evaluated ONCE per statement, but not here. The remaining cases are: a CONTINUOUSLY re-evaluated expression (`assign`, `force`, a `wait` condition) — the copy-out cannot re-fire on every change; an intra-assignment delay (`x = #1 f2(...)`); a `min:typ:max` or a constraint/`with` expression; any position inside a FUNCTION body lowered as a call frame (a function is entered from the expression that calls it, so it has no call statement of its own to carry the copy-out) — the same call in a TASK body, or in a module process, does work; and an evaluation-order case the hoist cannot preserve — an output actual read to the LEFT of the call when the actual is not a plain bit-vector net, when two calls in the same expression write it, or when a call the hoist leaves in place could read it (its body, or an OMITTED formal's default, or a method on a non-container receiver). Assign the call to a temporary first (`t = f2(...);`) and use `t`. [in top]
